WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.417
A shop sells to hundreds of credit customers each month. Posting every invoice to the sales account would take ages. So the sales day book lists them, and only its total is posted.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:29.295
Sales, purchases and expenses are nominal accounts. Sales is income, so its totals go on the credit side. Purchases and expenses go on the debit side, including each petty cash analysis column total.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:45.820
Put the opening balance on its normal side. Work out any book totals, for example the total to date plus new entries. Post each total on the same side, with the date and the name of the book. Leave out returns.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:01:00.826
Then close the account. For a year-end transfer, write income statement on the other side, so both sides total the same. If the question says balance the account, use balance carried down and brought down instead.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:19.167
Here is a real question from June 2023, Paper 1. The sales account balance on the first of March was seventy-one thousand seven hundred and thirty dollars. Prepare the sales account, showing the transfer to the income statement. Five marks.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:30.666
In March, Mitch sold goods on credit to Jay and to Mateta, Jay returned goods, and there was a cash sale of fifty dollars. The sales day book total to date was three thousand one hundred and ninety-four.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:38.898
Add the new credit sales to the total to date: three thousand one hundred and ninety-four, plus five hundred and seventy, plus three hundred and sixteen, is four thousand and eighty.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.326
Sales is income, so the opening balance goes on the credit side.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:52.633
Post the day book total and the cash sale, also on the credit side. Jay's return of eighty-five dollars goes to the sales returns account, not here.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:02:06.453
The credit side totals seventy-five thousand eight hundred and sixty. Transfer it to the income statement on the debit side, so both sides agree. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:16.063
A common mistake is debiting the sales day book total. Sales is income, so it is a credit.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:24.195
Another is writing balance carried down when the question asks for the transfer. The label must be income statement.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:36.323
Now you try. Read the data, then prepare the purchases account for May, showing the transfer to the income statement. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:51.521
The day book total is three thousand one hundred. The debit side is eighteen thousand four hundred, plus three thousand one hundred, plus ninety: twenty-one thousand five hundred and ninety. The return goes to the purchases returns account.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:03:01.334
Purchases is an expense, so the balance and the totals are debits. Twenty-one thousand five hundred and ninety is transferred to the income statement on the credit side.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:11.747
Remember: opening balance on its normal side, post the book totals on the same side, then close to the income statement. Now try the practice questions.
